syntax.chart:
JSON with a type, categories and series:
{"type": "bar", "categories": ["A", "B"], "series": [{"name": "Run 1", "values": [1, 2]}]}
Other types: line, area, scatter, pie, donut, histogram.

syntax.latex:
Display LaTeX, such as an equation or align environment:
\begin{align} a &= b + c \end{align}
Chemistry with \ce{H2O} and units with \pu{5 mg}.

syntax.tikz:
TikZ commands, or a whole tikzpicture:
{{example}}
Lines above the picture, such as \usetikzlibrary{positioning}, go in the preamble.

syntax.circuitikz:
CircuiTikZ commands, or a whole circuitikz environment:
{{example}}
Lines above the circuit, such as \ctikzset{resistors/scale=0.8}, go in the preamble.

syntax.jsx:
One React component file with a default export:
export default function App() { return <p>Hello</p> }
It can import react, recharts, d3, lodash, papaparse, chart.js and lucide-react.
